[{:db/id 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-45f3ee1a-e687-51c7-8953-3c231936ec3d" "question-0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" "question-88681796-21e9-5e72-a195-e1da66276721" "question-b4493b8f-a3b6-5d7e-9641-4ac3f05dd564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115075 :question/problem "Let ![](images/a9/a9f425a48a3ed8fabfce0eb1785ebdddc62d7dd3208ac302fd66a89b03e58cdb.svg) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83a65485-4098-56b8-8fd5-9fb601be0cb0" "question-f990568f-351a-543d-9726-4bfca20a8616" "question-4e584c32-a3dd-5eaa-a4dc-b23f04848d16" "question-cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115076 :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/11/11c345fde8fecb2e2a5459a0868ad8892e9067820de72f91601c1033858ca019.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-535f214d-c021-5eea-9acd-b13d4504df24" "question-338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115077 :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ea/ead4157a19d725334c44a55903b52bd12d7627e73696c2100efee52340347468.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ba/ba70270430d6c5606e816c16c606c8f3940742a48c95b0ad8a33f6c935da8cf6.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-45f3ee1a-e687-51c7-8953-3c231936ec3d" :question/id #uuid "45f3ee1a-e687-51c7-8953-3c231936ec3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75075" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-8$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}$ to $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a02475ca-ca51-5bbb-9fb2-8ed70c95ef71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a02475ca-ca51-5bbb-9fb2-8ed70c95ef71" :answer-field/id #uuid "a02475ca-ca51-5bbb-9fb2-8ed70c95ef71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eb024a6c-2255-51f9-a1ab-f1df1f59e9cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd6ef404-d51f-5dc8-8232-ced9b78b97ef" "answer-46c940ea-d23e-573b-94e4-9b08dcb0d527" "answer-4833bf41-8721-53ee-a05b-eef1d1d7ffbe" "answer-eb024a6c-2255-51f9-a1ab-f1df1f59e9cb" "answer-74604d91-78d7-5d75-a2b1-c1116cb378c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd6ef404-d51f-5dc8-8232-ced9b78b97ef" :answer/id #uuid "dd6ef404-d51f-5dc8-8232-ced9b78b97ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=8{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46c940ea-d23e-573b-94e4-9b08dcb0d527" :answer/id #uuid "46c940ea-d23e-573b-94e4-9b08dcb0d527" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-8){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4833bf41-8721-53ee-a05b-eef1d1d7ffbe" :answer/id #uuid "4833bf41-8721-53ee-a05b-eef1d1d7ffbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-8{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb024a6c-2255-51f9-a1ab-f1df1f59e9cb" :answer/id #uuid "eb024a6c-2255-51f9-a1ab-f1df1f59e9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74604d91-78d7-5d75-a2b1-c1116cb378c2" :answer/id #uuid "74604d91-78d7-5d75-a2b1-c1116cb378c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" :question/id #uuid "0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-130841" :question/problem "Let  $E=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-15$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-15{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3095f9c5-6e39-53cb-accf-8b0a4693c3a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3095f9c5-6e39-53cb-accf-8b0a4693c3a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "3095f9c5-6e39-53cb-accf-8b0a4693c3a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" "answer-6c046924-1709-5274-a794-1f3b95605dec" "answer-041b2509-a556-5b7c-ab45-9ca5fd9c3cc1" "answer-7e45231b-e9d5-5367-ad87-33c31af8b88a" "answer-08e24a6d-b6f5-53e0-a5c7-349a5368a361"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" :answer/id #uuid "7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c046924-1709-5274-a794-1f3b95605dec" :answer/id #uuid "6c046924-1709-5274-a794-1f3b95605dec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=15{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-041b2509-a556-5b7c-ab45-9ca5fd9c3cc1" :answer/id #uuid "041b2509-a556-5b7c-ab45-9ca5fd9c3cc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-15{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e45231b-e9d5-5367-ad87-33c31af8b88a" :answer/id #uuid "7e45231b-e9d5-5367-ad87-33c31af8b88a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-15{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08e24a6d-b6f5-53e0-a5c7-349a