math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-6){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0355739-0916-506f-b796-ffbe20c9beba" :answer/id #uuid "e0355739-0916-506f-b796-ffbe20c9beba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=(-6){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40cb2605-d7af-5bce-abf6-276350c8dc19" :answer/id #uuid "40cb2605-d7af-5bce-abf6-276350c8dc19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e0aec34-380f-59c7-b0b9-bab7ff9c5edb" :answer/id #uuid "2e0aec34-380f-59c7-b0b9-bab7ff9c5edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4493b8f-a3b6-5d7e-9641-4ac3f05dd564" :question/id #uuid "b4493b8f-a3b6-5d7e-9641-4ac3f05dd564" :question/math-academy-id "q-42759" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $5$ times the second row: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ea2baf5-4b46-568a-a3d6-feb9ec4d750b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ea2baf5-4b46-568a-a3d6-feb9ec4d750b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ea2baf5-4b46-568a-a3d6-feb9ec4d750b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f65184d9-bfa6-542f-9d5c-645cc46c8862" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fd22bfe-ec1d-572b-acb0-a9341c95ca1b" "answer-94c48f90-9bd5-5d16-a188-2cca931f231d" "answer-07e35b25-669e-55d1-afe7-e324171bb24a" "answer-f65184d9-bfa6-542f-9d5c-645cc46c8862" "answer-d191fc7a-1435-519a-aadd-42c211b37297"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fd22bfe-ec1d-572b-acb0-a9341c95ca1b" :answer/id #uuid "7fd22bfe-ec1d-572b-acb0-a9341c95ca1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94c48f90-9bd5-5d16-a188-2cca931f231d" :answer/id #uuid "94c48f90-9bd5-5d16-a188-2cca931f231d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07e35b25-669e-55d1-afe7-e324171bb24a" :answer/id #uuid "07e35b25-669e-55d1-afe7-e324171bb24a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f65184d9-bfa6-542f-9d5c-645cc46c8862" :answer/id #uuid "f65184d9-bfa6-542f-9d5c-645cc46c8862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d191fc7a-1435-519a-aadd-42c211b37297" :answer/id #uuid "d191fc7a-1435-519a-aadd-42c211b37297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83a65485-4098-56b8-8fd5-9fb601be0cb0" :question/id #uuid "83a65485-4098-56b8-8fd5-9fb601be0cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-75085" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix  multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2aac0eaa-471e-5dbe-b548-fdcceec82768"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2aac0eaa-471e-5dbe-b548-fdcceec82768" :answer-field/id #uuid "2aac0eaa-471e-5dbe-b548-fdcceec82768" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f0933af3-315c-5ed7-9e83-1579024a13fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d566eeb-c787-50d9-b13f-ce1b7120d3c6" "answer-cbc2c6fd-b284-52d1-a325-c376d492bf6b" "answer-20c9680f-b10b-5c24-9935-0c2f6390ac02" "answer-f0933af3-315c-5ed7-9e83-1579024a13fb" "answer-44e0513f-e37a-568a-ba3a-06d8338beab6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d566eeb-c787-50d9-b13f-ce1b7120d3c6" :answer/id #uuid "5d566eeb-c787-50d9-b13f-ce1b7120d3c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbc2c6fd-b284-52d1-a325-c376d492bf6b" :answer/id #uuid "cbc2c6fd-b284-52d1-a325-c376d492bf6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20c9680f-b10b-5c24-9935-0c2f6390ac02" :answer/id #uuid "20c9680f-b10b-5c24-9935-0c2f6390ac02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0933af3-315c-5ed7-9e83-1579024a13fb" :answer/id #uuid "f0933af3-315c-5ed7-9e83-1579024a13fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44e0513f-e37a-568a-ba3a-06d8338beab6" :answer/id #uuid "44e0513f-e37a-568a-ba3a-06d8338beab6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f990568f-351a-543d-9726-4bfca20a8616" :question/id #uuid "f990568f-351a-543d-9726-4bfca20a8616" :question/math-academy-id "q-75087" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$  \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb2a33dc-019b-539c-8057-1ac05dffb007"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb2a33dc-019b-539c-8057-1ac05dffb007" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2a33dc-019b-539c-8057-1ac05dffb007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-06e05fbe-65fb-57d3-abc5-dad8fbda182c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3d9b0b9-9afc-539b-a11d-4895134d5d0f" "answer-b123dd5a-7531-527b-b537-ac54ff7d5dfc" "answer-06e05fbe-65fb-57d3-abc5-dad8fbda182c" "answer-13ff5b43-6d2d-5974-abfa-8944682722ee" "answer-4e3f1fc6-8f02-5a4d-8369-6a8d56c223fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3d9b0b9-9afc-539b-a11d-4895134d5d0f" :answer/id #uuid "a3d9b0b9-9afc-539b-a11d-4895134d5d0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\