uestion.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76248571-5036-5758-846c-eda5b7a6680e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76248571-5036-5758-846c-eda5b7a6680e" :answer-field/id #uuid "76248571-5036-5758-846c-eda5b7a6680e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-86b0d865-71ce-5220-9638-642262d571c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bdc6917-9114-570c-b655-0097a2be410a" "answer-f6c7a979-ff9d-5864-b885-40fddca4b43c" "answer-e3990169-9d67-57a7-8327-43a5424638ed" "answer-afc0ce32-cc50-5733-b5e8-eadc123226ec" "answer-86b0d865-71ce-5220-9638-642262d571c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bdc6917-9114-570c-b655-0097a2be410a" :answer/id #uuid "6bdc6917-9114-570c-b655-0097a2be410a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6c7a979-ff9d-5864-b885-40fddca4b43c" :answer/id #uuid "f6c7a979-ff9d-5864-b885-40fddca4b43c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3990169-9d67-57a7-8327-43a5424638ed" :answer/id #uuid "e3990169-9d67-57a7-8327-43a5424638ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afc0ce32-cc50-5733-b5e8-eadc123226ec" :answer/id #uuid "afc0ce32-cc50-5733-b5e8-eadc123226ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86b0d865-71ce-5220-9638-642262d571c7" :answer/id #uuid "86b0d865-71ce-5220-9638-642262d571c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e" :question/id #uuid "cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75088" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3bba64a8-5bb2-5bab-90e3-aa7ac4488ef1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3bba64a8-5bb2-5bab-90e3-aa7ac4488ef1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bba64a8-5bb2-5bab-90e3-aa7ac4488ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-487debef-ed20-58c1-b2bb-36f8c9abf586" "answer-0f089b50-55e5-516b-9f45-db7bc3a03d01" "answer-6e60ea78-a600-5e26-8bc9-6dc62c40ffde" "answer-a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" "answer-08df48ed-79af-5bf2-85ef-d1439433ab47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-487debef-ed20-58c1-b2bb-36f8c9abf586" :answer/id #uuid "487debef-ed20-58c1-b2bb-36f8c9abf586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f089b50-55e5-516b-9f45-db7bc3a03d01" :answer/id #uuid "0f089b50-55e5-516b-9f45-db7bc3a03d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e60ea78-a600-5e26-8bc9-6dc62c40ffde" :answer/id #uuid "6e60ea78-a600-5e26-8bc9-6dc62c40ffde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" :answer/id #uuid "a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08df48ed-79af-5bf2-85ef-d1439433ab47" :answer/id #uuid "08df48ed-79af-5bf2-85ef-d1439433ab47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-535f214d-c021-5eea-9acd-b13d4504df24" :question/id #uuid "535f214d-c021-5eea-9acd-b13d4504df24" :question/math-academy-id "q-31977" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef5c36a4-d082-5926-820f-4cd3513e1032"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef5c36a4-d082-5926-820f-4cd3513e1032" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef5c36a4-d082-5926-820f-4cd3513e1032" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e1ac934-f42e-5421-a48c-557b71cea666" "answer-f88a4afc-f340-5d8a-8f8b-7f4abe4ed444" "answer-f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" "answer-ab7860a0-b9d2-5afc-af0b-2703b7594661" "answer-3e96febe-54c3-5e3a-a3b3-7bd0082d0748"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e1ac934-f42e-5421-a48c-557b71cea666" :answer/id #uuid "9e1ac934-f42e-5421-a48c-557b71cea666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f88a4afc-f340-5d8a-8f8b-7f4abe4ed444" :answer/id #uuid "f88a4afc-f340-5d8a-8f8b-7f4abe4ed444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" :answer/id #uuid "f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab7860a0-b9d2-5afc-af0b-2703b7594661" :answer/id #uuid "ab7860a0-b9d2-5afc-af0b-2703b7594661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e96febe-54c3-5e3a-a3b3-7bd0082d0748" :answer/id #uuid "3e96febe-54c3-5e3a-a3b3-7bd0082d0748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770" :question/id #uuid "338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770" :question/math-academy-id "q-130863" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}=7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98133f54-d0b4-500e-be6b-d23f4be79f09"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98133f54-d0b4-500e-be6b-d23f4be79f09" :answer-field/id #uuid "98133f54-d0b4-500e-be6b-d23f4be79f09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc6c5718-69bf-54af-9c04-7a6648adfb74" "answer-7a31368e-5bda-5127-82e3-a85cb11c6a79" "answer-0e2034d0-7cda-5f39-9589-90aba5659d9e" "answer-4d910c4e-a0ac-50d5-9159-50d27df48002" "answer-49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc6c5718-69bf-54af-9c04-7a6648adfb74" :answer/id #uuid "bc6c5718-69bf-54af-9c04-7a6648adfb74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a31368e-5bda-5127-82e3-a85cb11c6a79" :answer/id #uuid "7a31368e-5bda-5127-82e3-a85cb11c6a79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e2034d0-7cda-5f39-9589-90aba5659d9e" :answer/id #uuid "0e2034d0-7cda-5f39-9589-90aba5659d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d910c4e-a0ac-50d5-9159-50d27df48002" :answer/id #uuid "4d910c4e-a0ac-50d5-9159-50d27df48002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2" :answer/id #uuid "49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116497 :tutorial/content "To compute the product of an elementary matrix and another matrix, one option is to perform the matrix multiplication as usual. However, there's an easier, quicker way.\n\nRemember that every elementary matrix is the result of applying an elementary row operation to the identity matrix. If we multiply another matrix by an elementary matrix, we're effectively applying the elementary row operation to the other matrix.\n\nFor example, suppose we are asked to find the product $EA$ where\n![](images/25/25d4c31649834fe3ae42a701d49f6e4a31fa8626de1d9aeed0f98ccbbf4a57fb.svg)\n\nThe elementary matrix $E$ comes from swapping the two rows of the identity matrix ($R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$). So, to compute the product $EA,$ all we have to do is swap the two rows of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/49/497b76accb211bbe4253ee2094206f70e8856f9510db71f6367f255fcc565665.svg)\n\nThis may seem almost too easy. But it's true! And we can verify it by computing the product the long way, using matrix multiplication. Indeed, we get the same result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we say that $E \\cdot A$ is equivalent to applying to $A$ the elementary row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$\n\n**Watch out!** It's important to multiply $A$ from the *left*. If we multiply $A$ by an elementary matrix from the *right*, we will perform a *column* operation on $A$ (not a row operation). In this case, multiplying $A$ by $E$ from the right will have the effect of switching the *columns* of $A,$ not the rows.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AE & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115473 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
